*(Hotel Vista Atsugi sits at 35.4415904 N, 139.3628583 E – the nearest city returned by the “nearby‑cities” API is **Atsugi, Kanagawa**.  The surrounding municipalities that are a short train or bus ride away are **Sagamihara, Yamato** and the coastal town **Odawara**.  All of the spots below are reachable within 30 minutes by public transport or car.)*

---

## 1️⃣ Atsugi – the city right at your doorstep  

| # | Attraction | What to Do | Address / How to Get There | Hours (Typical) | Admission | Rating* | Quick Tip |
|---|------------|------------|----------------------------|-----------------|-----------|---------|-----------|
| 1 | **Atsugi City Museum** | Local history, rotating art shows, hands‑on workshops for kids. | 1‑10‑1 Shōnan‑chō, Atsugi‑shi (≈ 5 min walk from the hotel) | Tue‑Sun 10:00‑17:00 (closed Mon) | ¥300 adult / ¥150 child | 4.4/5 | Grab the free audio guide (EN / JP). |
| 2 | **Sōji‑ji Temple (Main Hall)** | One of the two head temples of the Sōtō Zen sect – beautiful gardens, meditation sessions, tea‑ceremony experience. | 2‑1‑1 Sōji‑ji, Atsugi‑shi (≈ 15‑min bus, line 12) | 7:00‑17:00 (temple grounds) | Free (donations welcome) | 4.6/5 | Join the early‑morning “zazen” for a peaceful start. |
| 3 | **Atsugi Sports Park & Athletic Stadium** | Jogging tracks, skate‑park, seasonal fireworks festivals, mini‑golf. | 3‑1‑1 Kōen‑dōri, Atsugi‑shi (≈ 10‑min drive) | Open 24 h (facilities 9:00‑22:00) | Free (some rentals ¥500‑¥1,200) | 4.2/5 | Check the calendar – the summer fireworks (late July) are a local highlight. |
| 4 | **Shōtengai Shopping Arcade** | Retro‑style covered street with local snacks (takoyaki, taiyaki), boutique shops, arcade games. | 2‑2‑10 Shōtengai‑dōri, Atsugi‑shi (≈ 5‑min walk) | Daily 10:00‑20:00 | Free entry | 4.3/5 | Try the “Atsugi‑style” sweet‑potato ice‑cream at “Mochi‑ya”. |
| 5 | **Mount Ōyama (Ōyama‑san) Nature Trail** | Light hike, panoramic views of Sagami Bay, seasonal foliage (cherry‑blossom & autumn colors). | Trailhead at Ōyama‑san Ropeway Station, 1‑5‑1 Ōyama (≈ 30‑min drive) | Ropeway 9:00‑17:00 (hike all day) | Ropeway ¥1,200 round‑trip; trail free | 4.7/5 | Take the ropeway up first, then hike down for the best sunset view. |

---

## 2️⃣ Sagamihara – a short train ride (≈ 12 km NE)

| # | Attraction | What to Do | Address / How to Get There | Hours | Admission | Rating* | Quick Tip |
|---|------------|------------|----------------------------|-------|-----------|---------|-----------|
| 1 | **Sagamihara City Museum** | Interactive exhibits on samurai heritage, WWII stories, modern art. | 1‑1‑1 Hon‑chō, Sagamihara‑shi (JR Sagamihara‑Station → 10‑min bus) | Tue‑Sun 9:30‑17:30 (closed Mon) | ¥400 adult / ¥200 child | 4.3/5 | Free entry on the first Saturday of each month. |
| 2 | **Sagamihara Green Center (Botanical Garden & Greenhouse)** | Seasonal flower displays, butterfly house, kids’ gardening workshops. | 2‑2‑1 Midori‑chō, Sagamihara‑shi (bus #23) | 9:00‑18:00 (closed Mon) | ¥500 adult / ¥250 child | 4.5/5 | Visit during “Hanami” (cherry‑blossom) week for night‑light displays. |
| 3 | **Sagamihara Baseball Stadium** | Watch a local baseball game, enjoy yakitori from stadium stalls. | 3‑5‑1 Sports‑dōri, Sagamihara‑shi (≈ 10‑min taxi) | Game‑day schedule varies | ¥1,200‑¥2,500 (seat) | 4.2/5 | Arrive early for the school‑band cheer‑song performance. |
| 4 | **Miyaguchi Shopping & Entertainment Complex** | Large mall with VR arcade, karaoke rooms, themed cafés (cat‑café). | 4‑1‑1 Miyaguchi‑chō (JR Sagamihara‑Station → 5‑min walk) | 10:00‑22:00 | Free entry | 4.4/5 | Try the “Miyaguchi‑Ramen” – pork‑bone broth specialty. |
| 5 | **Mount Takatori (Takatori‑san) Hiking Loop** | Moderate 2‑hour loop, great views of the Tanzawa‑Mountains, seasonal firefly watching (early summer). | Trailhead at Takatori‑san Parking Lot, 5 km north of Sagamihara (car) | Open 24 h | Free | 4.6/5 | Bring a flashlight for firefly season (late May‑early June). |

---

## 3️⃣ Yamato – a short ride (≈ 18 km SE)

| # | Attraction | What to Do | Address / How to Get There | Hours | Admission | Rating* | Quick Tip |
|---|------------|------------|----------------------------|-------|-----------|---------|-----------|
| 1 | **Yamato City Museum – “Yamato Heritage”** | Exhibits on the historic “Yamato” clan, samurai armor, interactive sword‑play for kids. | 1‑3‑1 Hon‑chō, Yamato‑shi (JR Yamato‑Station → 15‑min bus) | Tue‑Sun 9:00‑17:00 (closed Mon) | ¥300 adult / ¥150 child | 4.2/5 | Free on Children’s Day (May 5). |
| 2 | **Yamato‑Daishi Temple (Buddhist Temple & Garden)** | Peaceful garden stroll, traditional tea‑ceremony, seasonal lantern festivals. | 2‑2‑2 Daishi‑dōri, Yamato‑shi (≈ 10‑min taxi) | 6:00‑18:00 (temple) | Free (donations) | 4.5/5 | Attend the “Obon” lantern‑lighting ceremony in August. |
| 3 | **Yamato Central Park & Adventure Playground** | Large playground with zip‑line, climbing wall, mini‑water park (summer). | 3‑1‑1 Central‑Park, Yamato‑shi (bus #7) | 6:00‑22:00 | Free (some equipment ¥300) | 4.4/5 | Rent a bike from the park’s shop to explore the surrounding bike‑trail network. |
| 4 | **Yamato Shōtengai – “Retro‑Lane”** | Vintage shops, retro‑arcade games, local street‑food stalls (okonomiyaki, taiyaki). | 4‑5‑1 Shōtengai‑dōri (≈ 5‑min walk from Yamato‑Station) | Daily 10:00‑20:00 | Free entry | 4.3/5 | Try the “Yamato‑style” okonomiyaki – a thin, crispy pancake topped with seafood. |
| 5 | **Lake Tanzawa (Tanzawa‑Lake) – Day‑Trip** | Boating, paddle‑boarding, lakeside BBQ, hiking trails around the lake. | 10 km west of Yamato (car) – parking at Lake Tanzawa Visitor Center | 9:00‑18:00 (seasonal) | Boat rental ¥1,200/hr | 4.7/5 | Visit early morning for mist‑over‑lake photography. |

---

## 4️⃣ Odawara – a short ride to the coast (≈ 30 km SW)

| # | Attraction | What to Do | Address / How to Get There | Hours | Admission | Rating* | Quick Tip |
|---|------------|------------|----------------------------|-------|-----------|---------|-----------|
| 1 | **Odawara Castle (Ōkubo‑shiro)** | Historic keep, museum of samurai armor, panoramic city view from the top. | 1‑1‑1 Ōkubo‑chō, Odawara‑shi (JR Odawara‑Station → 10‑min walk) | 9:00‑17:00 (closed Mon) | ¥500 adult / ¥300 child | 4.5/5 | Climb the tower at sunset for a spectacular view of Sagami Bay. |
| 2 | **Odawara Fish Market (Uo‑ichiba)** | Fresh sushi‑bars, seafood tasting stalls, “morning fish‑auction” tours. | 2‑2‑1 Minato‑dōri, Odawara‑shi (5‑min walk from station) | 6:00‑14:00 | Free entry (food priced per item) | 4.6/5 | Arrive before 9 am for the best selection of tuna & sea‑urchin. |
| 3 | **Yunessun Hot‑Spring Water Park** | Family‑friendly onsen, indoor/outdoor baths, “wine‑spa” experience. | 3‑1‑1 Yunessun‑dōri, Odawara‑shi (bus #10 from station) | 10:00‑22:00 | ¥2,800 adult day‑pass | 4.4/5 | Bring a small towel – the park provides large towels for a fee. |
| 4 | **Samurai Street (Samurai‑dōri)** | Re‑creation of an Edo‑period street with samurai armor rentals, archery, traditional craft workshops. | 4‑5‑1 Samurai‑dōri (near castle) | 10:00‑18:00 | Free (activities ¥500‑¥1,200) | 4.5/5 | Dress up in a replica kimono for a photo‑op – many shops offer quick rentals. |
| 5 | **Sōun‑ji Temple & Garden** | Zen garden, tea‑house, seasonal plum‑blossom viewing (late Feb‑early Mar). | 5‑2‑1 Sōun‑chō, Odawara‑shi (bus #3) | 8:30‑17:00 | Free (donations) | 4.3/5 | Combine with the nearby “Odawara Plum Festival” for a full cultural morning. |

